        <body>
            <div xml:id="d190">

                <pb facs="0452" n="420" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v02/pg420"/>

                <head>190. Memorandum From the Deputy Director for Intelligence, Central
                    Intelligence Agency (Cline) to
                    the President’s Special Assistant for National Security Affairs (Bundy)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d190-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1965-03-08">March 8,
                    1965</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Vietnam</item>
                </list>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Herewith my own capsule appreciation of the unfolding of the scenario in
                        Vietnam so far. It is in accord with the views of most of my Southeast Asia
                        experts but is far too clear-cut a statement to be coordinated easily as an
                        official intelligence community view.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>For your noting, not necessarily for reading, are two of my earlier
                            memos<anchor n="2" xml:id="d190-f2"/> on the situation in Vietnam and
                        what to do about it. You will see I am at least consistent. My only fear now
                        is that we may have waited too long to reduce the pressure on the political
                        and internal security fabric in South Vietnam. It is pretty threadbare, as
                        you know. If it holds, then I believe the course we are on will pay
                        dividends as time goes on.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Ray S. Cline</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d190-a1.xml" xpointer="d190-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
